pec.md:741:- **FR-013** (MUST): The vendored unittest suite MUST pass via `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` from the plugin root. Doc-contract assertions MUST be migrated, not deleted: each of the 24 upstream assertions is either retained (engine prose unchanged), updated to the merged skill/doc text, or removed with a line in `UPSTREAM` naming the assertion and why.\n97d4d60:docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:872:Revision-13 sharded-cell amendment to **FR-149** (bead forge-plugin-pwy): an executable policy cell MAY fan its work out over internal parallel worker processes, provided every worker is a descendant of the cell's `bash -c` process (so the runner's isolated process group, kill-on-timeout, and fixed 1200-second bound cover them all), the cell itself fails closed on any worker failure or missing result, and the cell keeps its combined stdout plus stderr within the 65,536-byte cap by emitting bounded per-worker tails. The runner discipline is unchanged: one cell as one argv element, `forge` as `$0`, parameters through `\"$@\"`, no concatenation or interpolation. This repository's `gate1-test-command` cell applies it: full unittest discovery of `tests/test_*.py` partitioned round-robin over `min(4, cpu)` shards, refusing an empty module set, a nonzero shard, or a shard without a final unittest summary, and printing at most the last 8 KiB of each shard. FR-013's plain `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` remains the vendored-suite contract and must still pass; the sharded cell collects the same modules.\n97d4d60:docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:1466:- **FR-242** (MUST): Phase-5 marker-deletion admission is a conjunction, not authority to delete. A later control revision MAY propose deletion only when one mechanically recorded candidate proves all eleven predicates: (1) release/manifests and executable compatibility tests prove phase-1 dual-accept shipped before phase 3 and was never bypassed in the supported upgrade lineage; (2) committed DM-015 is `forge-verbs-v1`; (3) the recorded DM-016 hashes prove every v1 corpus/eval/manifest byte unchanged; (4) v2 reason, matcher, merge-transition, matrix, recovery, push, cleanup, and activated-denial eval/test results all PASS; (5) every merge-finalize and push last-line check has a focused disable-in-memory test that fails on its mutant; (6) `STRICT=1` evals PASS; (7) full unittest discovery PASSes twice consecutively and serially after the candidate's last fix, with each suite's own tail retained; (8) a closed inventory scan of installed skills, templates, hooks, CLI help, rendered close protocol, and routing proves none produces raw commit/push or marker authorization; (9) an atomic scan under the applicable locks proves no nonterminal legacy chain and no unexpired DM-006 marker remains consumable; (10) marker grammar, parser, and tests remained present through the complete phase-4 candidate; and (11) the exact deletion candidate receives binding independent PASS and explicit operator approval. Missing, unavailable, stale, or non-PASS evidence makes the predicate false. Revision 7 does not authorize deletion, and a phase-5 implementation MUST preserve compatibility for every supported repository that has not yet proven activation rather than globally removing its only admission path.\n97d4d60:docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:3104:- Vendored suite green: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` (state/monitor/validation/replay/docs-contract/report-skill/version)\n97d4d60:docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:3142:- Every required serial suite record is judged from that suite's own output tail, never a background wrapper's exit code; after the last defect fix, applicable end-to-end checks follow FR-121 and full unittest discovery passes twice consecutively before phase-5 admission can be claimed\n97d4d60:docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:3151:- **SC-001**: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 from the plugin root on macOS and Linux with bare Python ≥ 3.10 (no packages insta